### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### 04a - AGENT DELEGATION (Phase 76)
###
### The Coordinator (Vishnu) delegates complex tasks to domain-expert
### sub-agents via the `garuda` tool. This file covers:
###
###   A. Happy path: coordinator → each specialist (all 11 agents)
###   B. Deity alias resolution in delegation (shiva, brahma, datta, brahaspati, etc.)
###   C. DelegationRoutingProvider fast-path intent routing
###      ("ask shiva to...", "tell brahma to...", "have the synthesizer...")
###   D. Guard rails: self-delegation, unknown agent, blank parameters
###   E. Role-capability enforcement: non-coordinator roles blocked (403)
###   F. GitHub misuse guard (ToolStepHandler Component 5)
###   G. Inner session checkpoint isolation (":d:" prefix rows)
###   H. Repeated delegation - unique inner session IDs (collision fix)
###   I. Loop exceeded and budget propagation
###   J. Self-contained goal quality: vague "fix it" must be rephrased
###   K. Negative routing: phrases that must NOT trigger delegation
###
### Delegation capability matrix (Phase 76):
###   COORDINATOR  → has garuda ✓
###   RESEARCHER   → blocked (403 ROLE_CAPABILITY_MISMATCH)
###   CODER        → blocked (403) + empty tool schema (structural)
###   DEBUGGER     → blocked (403)
###   ARCHITECT    → blocked (403)
###   SYNTHESIZER  → blocked (403)
###
### Inner session ID pattern (after collision fix):
###   {outerSessionId}:d:{agentRole}:{8-char-uuid-prefix}
###
### Hindu deity aliases accepted by garuda 'agent' param:
###   "vishnu"      → COORDINATOR (self-delegation → 400)
###   "coordinator" → COORDINATOR (self-delegation → 400)
###   "brahma"      → CODER
###   "shiva"       → DEBUGGER
###   "saraswati"   → RESEARCHER
###   "brihaspati" / "brahaspati" → ARCHITECT
###   "dattatreya" / "datta"      → SYNTHESIZER
###   "ganesha" / "ganesh"        → OPTIMIZER
###   "kartikeya" / "murugan" / "skanda" → SENTINEL
###   "lakshmi"     → HEALER
###   "durga"       → PROTECTOR
###   "kali"        → PURIFIER
###   "parvati" / "uma" → NURTURER
###
### Prerequisites: ArcClaw serve mode, ARCCLAW_LLM_API_KEY set.
###   GitHub tool tests additionally require GITHUB_TOKEN in vault.
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# @baseUrl  = http://localhost:8080
# @validKey = key-internal-cWevfEoRvstUv0PqGpf02LzDY5kPNaz1y9GSl0LZOwU=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SECTION A - HAPPY PATH: COORDINATOR → EACH SPECIALIST
# Each test: coordinator session → explicit delegation goal →
# verify sub-agent result is returned as coordinator's final answer.
# Logs to check: TOOL_INVOKED(garuda), inner session with
# ":d:{role}:" prefix present in StatefulAgentStore checkpoint rows.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [DEL-1] Create coordinator session for happy-path tests
# @name delSession
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

### [DEL-2] Coordinator → Shiva (Debugger): stack trace delegation
# Expect 200 Finished: Shiva's root cause analysis via coordinator.
# Logs: TOOL_INVOKED(garuda), role=coordinator outer,
# inner checkpoint keyed on {sessionId}:d:debugger:{uuid}.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{delSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "Delegate to shiva: analyze this NullPointerException and give the most likely root cause.\njava.lang.NullPointerException: Cannot invoke String.length() because str is null\n  at com.example.OrderService.processOrder(OrderService.java:88)\n  at com.example.OrderController.submit(OrderController.java:34)",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 5
}

###

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{delSession.response.body.sessionId}}/status/coordinator
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{delSession.response.body.sessionId}}/approve?agentRole=coordinator
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

