# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SECTION C - DelegationRoutingProvider FAST-PATH INTENT ROUTING
# Natural language phrases like "ask shiva to...", "tell brahma to..."
# must route to COORDINATOR (not directly to the specialist) via
# DelegationRoutingProvider at priority 5 in IntentDetectorService.
# The coordinator then uses garuda internally.
# agentRole is omitted so the intent classifier decides the route.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [DEL-12] Create session for intent routing tests (no agentRole in request)
# @name intentSession
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

### [DEL-13] "ask shiva to..." → fast-path → coordinator → delegates to debugger
# Expect 200: DelegationRoutingProvider fires, role=coordinator in logs,
# coordinator calls garuda(agent="shiva").
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{intentSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "Ask shiva to explain why a ConcurrentModificationException occurs in Java and how to fix it.",
    "maxIterations": 5
}

###

### [DEL-14] "tell brahma to..." → fast-path → coordinator → delegates to coder
